        "id": "exam-help-vs-tutoring-vs-tech-support",
        "title": "4. Online Exam Help vs Tutoring vs Technical Support",
        "content": "\n        <p>Understanding the boundaries between academic tutoring, pre-exam technical guidance, and official vendor support ensures you contact the right resource:</p>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Academic Tutoring:</strong> Focuses on learning subject matter, formulas, and question-solving techniques before test day.</li>\n          <li><strong>Pre-Exam Technical Guidance:</strong> Focuses on verifying laptop hardware, webcam/mic privacy settings, and background process conflicts prior to launching your test.</li>\n          <li><strong>Official Institutional / Vendor Support:</strong> Contact testing vendor helpdesks (such as <a href=\"https://home.pearsonvue.com/onvue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pearson VUE OnVUE</a>, <a href=\"https://www.pmi.org/certifications/process\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PMI Exam Policies</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.comptia.org/testing/testing-policies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CompTIA Testing Policies</a>) or your university IT desk for account password resets, candidate information bulletins, or active test disconnects during an exam session.</li>\n        </ul>\n      "
