    "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1581092160607-ee22621dd758?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
    "focusKeyword": "Respondus LockDown Browser student guide",
    "metaTitle": "Respondus LockDown Browser: Download & Student Setup Guide | TUTOR PROCTORED EXAMS",
    "metaDescription": "Respondus LockDown Browser student guide: find institution download links, Canvas/Blackboard setup, webcam checks, and technical support options.",
    "excerpt": "Step-by-step student guide for Respondus LockDown Browser downloads, Canvas/Blackboard quiz launches, camera permission setup, and pre-exam readiness checks.",
    "intro": "Respondus LockDown Browser is a specialized, secure web browser used by colleges and universities to lock down the computer environment during online assessments in Canvas, Blackboard, Brightspace, and Moodle. When LockDown Browser is active, students cannot print, copy, access external websites, or run secondary desktop applications. While LockDown Browser secures your local desktop, Respondus Monitor is an optional automated add-on that records webcam video and audio. This student guide outlines how to obtain your institution-specific download link, complete pre-exam system checks, launch LMS quizzes, and obtain official technical support.",
